UI Steering Profile: Neo-Bento Design System (ui-steering.md)
This steering document governs all frontend layout, component styling, and visual architecture generated by AI coding agents. The UI must strictly adhere to the Neo-Bento aesthetic—a hybrid design system that combines the structural, data-dense organization of Bento Box layouts with the tactile, soft-surface elevation of Neumorphism (Soft UI).

Place this file in your project root (e.g., /.kiro/ui-steering.md or root /ui-steering.md) so the AI agent references it during all frontend generation tasks.

1. Core Aesthetic Identity: "Neo-Bento"
Bento Box Structure: All page layouts, dashboards, and views must be compartmentalized into clean, asymmetric, responsive CSS grids. Every distinct data point, tool, or action lives inside its own dedicated "cell" or card.

Neumorphic Surfaces: Elements do not float above the background with hard drop-shadows. Instead, they appear to be physically extruded from (raised) or depressed into (inset) the background surface using paired light and dark shadows.

The Golden Rule of Neumorphism: The background color of an extruded or depressed component MUST exactly match the background color of its parent container. Contrast is achieved through shadow manipulation and typography, not surface color differences.

2. Color Palette & Shadow Engine
Neumorphism fails without exact tonal coordination. Do not invent random background colors; strictly use the following designated palette and shadow tokens (configured for Tailwind CSS / CSS Variables).

Standard Theme (Soft Slate / Light)
Base Canvas / Page BG: #e8ecf2 (Soft cool grey)

Surface BG (Cards, Buttons, Inputs): #e8ecf2 (Must match Canvas exactly)

Primary Text: #1e293b (Slate-800 - High contrast for accessibility)

Secondary Text: #64748b (Slate-500)

Accent Color: #2563eb (Blue-600 - Used sparingly for active states, primary CTAs, and progress indicators)

Shadow Formulas (Tailwind Arbitrary Values)
When generating components, apply these exact shadow physics:

Extruded Surface (Cards / Panels / Untoggled Buttons):

shadow-[8px_8px_16px_#cbced1,-8px_-8px_16px_#ffffff]

Depressed / Inset Surface (Inputs / Wells / Active Toggles):

shadow-[inset_4px_4px_8px_#cbced1,inset_-4px_-4px_8px_#ffffff]

Floating / Hover State (Subtle Lift):

shadow-[12px_12px_20px_#cbced1,-12px_-12px_20px_#ffffff]

3. Bento Grid Layout Architecture
When building dashboards, screens, or content containers, follow these structural grid rules:

Grid Foundation: Use CSS Grid via Tailwind classes: grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6 p-6.

Asymmetric Spanning: Vary card spans to create a true Bento hierarchy. Important metrics or hero controls should span multiple columns or rows.

Hero/Primary Card: col-span-1 md:col-span-2 lg:col-span-2 row-span-2

Quick Metric/Stat Cell: col-span-1 row-span-1

Wide Data Feed / Table Cell: col-span-1 md:col-span-3 lg:col-span-4 row-span-2

Gaps and Margins: Maintain consistent, generous spacing (gap-6 or gap-8) between cells so the neumorphic shadows do not collide or visually bleed into adjacent cards.

4. Component-Specific Implementation Rules
A. Bento Cards & Containers
Geometry: Generous border radii are mandatory. Use rounded-2xl or rounded-3xl for all Bento cells.

Surface: Apply the Extruded Surface shadow. Do not use standard 1px borders unless using a subtle `<0.05 opacity white inner stroke for edge definition.

Padding: Internal card padding must be spacious (p-6 or p-8).

B. Interactive Buttons
Default State: Extruded Surface (shadow-[6px_6px_12px_#cbced1,-6px_-6px_12px_#ffffff]) with rounded-xl, matching #e8ecf2 background, and bold primary text.

Hover State: Smooth transition (transition-all duration-200) to a slightly intensified lift or subtle accent text coloration.

Active / Pressed State: When clicked or toggled on, the button must physically depress into the canvas by switching instantly to the Inset Shadow: active:shadow-[inset_3px_3px_6px_#cbced1,inset_-3px_-3px_6px_#ffffff].

Primary CTA Buttons: For primary actions (e.g., "Approve", "Scan QR"), you may break pure neumorphism by applying the Accent BG Color (#2563eb) with a soft colored glow: bg-blue-600 text-white shadow-[0_8px_16px_rgba(37,99,235,0.3)] hover:bg-blue-500.

C. Input Fields & Data Wells
Text Inputs / Selects / Search Bars: Must always look like carved-out depressions in the Bento card.

Styling: Use bg-[#e8ecf2] rounded-xl p-4 shadow-[inset_3px_3px_6px_#cbced1,inset_-3px_-3px_6px_#ffffff] outline-none.

Focus State: When focused, do not change the background color. Add a subtle accent focus ring: focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500/50.

Data Readouts (Wells): For static readouts (like an extracted OCR JSON code block or account balance display), place them inside an inset well to visually separate them from interactive card controls.

D. Badges & Indicators
Keep badges minimal. Use pill shapes (rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold) with subtle inset backgrounds and high-contrast colored text (e.g., text-emerald-600 for Success, text-amber-600 for Pending, text-rose-600 for AML Risk).

5. Accessibility & Contrast Guardrails (Mandatory)
Pure neumorphism is frequently criticized for poor accessibility and low contrast. You must strictly enforce these safety overrides:

Never Rely on Shadows for Text/Icons: Text, icons, and essential informational graphics must NEVER be rendered using neumorphic shadows. They must use high-contrast solid colors (#1e293b or #64748b).

Explicit Focus States: Keyboard navigation and accessibility readers must be supported. Every interactive element must display a distinct, high-contrast outline or ring (focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-600) when navigated via keyboard.

Form Input Labels: Always provide explicit, high-contrast labels above or beside inset input fields. Never rely solely on placeholder text inside a depressed well.

6. Frontend Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)
🚫 NO Flat White/Black Cards: Do not generate standard cards with bg-white shadow-md or bg-slate-900. This destroys the neumorphic extrusion effect.

🚫 NO Random Background Gradients: Do not use rainbow or multi-color background gradients on Bento cells. The canvas and surface colors must remain flat and uniform to let the physics of the shadows work.

🚫 NO Sharp Corners: Never use rounded-none, rounded-sm, or rounded-md on layout containers. Neo-Bento requires organic, soft curves (rounded-2xl minimum for cards).

🚫 NO Cluttered Layouts: Do not stack 10 small elements vertically in a single column. Break data out into distinct Bento grid cells. If a screen feels cluttered, split it into additional grid spans.